<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/015T">Remark <span data-tag="015T">4.3.1.5</span>.</a> Variant <a data-tag="015S" href="/tag/015S">4.3.1.4</a> is formally dual to Construction <a data-tag="015P" href="/tag/015P">4.3.1.1</a>. More precisely, if $S$ is an object of a category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, then we have a canonical isomorphism of categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  (\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/S})^{\operatorname{op}} \simeq (\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}})_{S/}, \]
</div>
<p> where we view $S$ also as an object of the opposite category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}}$. </p>
